            <ArticleTitle>Chronic meningococcaemia: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>102-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic meningococcaemia (CM), caused by the bacterium Neisseria meningitidis is reported in a 27-year-old Indonesian man. The main symptoms were intermittent fever, skin rash and arthralgia. The pathogenesis, symptoms, differential diagnoses and treatment of CM are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
